# Copy to .env and uncomment the line that matches your setup. Compose
# (docker compose, podman-compose, podman compose) loads .env from this
# directory automatically -- no need to `export` anything by hand.
#
# Only needed under Podman -- Docker's default (/var/run/docker.sock)
# already works with no .env at all. See the "Running under Podman"
# section of README.md for the full setup (enabling the socket first,
# etc.) -- this file only covers which path to point at.
#
# .env files aren't shell-expanded, so for the rootless case below, run
# `echo $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` first and paste its actual value in (typically
# /run/user/<your-uid>) rather than leaving the variable reference as-is.

# CONTAINER_ENGINE_SOCKET=/run/user/1000/podman/podman.sock   # rootless (typical) -- replace 1000 with your uid
# CONTAINER_ENGINE_SOCKET=/run/podman/podman.sock             # rootful

# Only for docker-compose.prod.yml (TLS) -- host paths to the cert (full
# chain: this host's cert + any intermediate CA certs) and key nginx
# should terminate TLS with. Defaults to the throwaway pair
# scripts/gen-dev-cert.sh writes; point these at real files instead. See
# README.md's "HTTPS / TLS" section.
#
# If the real cert/key are root-owned system files (e.g. under
# /etc/pki/tls/, as on most RHEL/CentOS hosts) and this runs under
# *rootless* Podman, pointing straight at them like the commented-out
# example below will fail (unreadable, and the :z SELinux relabel can't
# touch a file you don't own) -- run scripts/sync-tls-cert.sh first and
# point these at its output instead (rootful Podman doesn't have this
# problem; see the README section for that alternative). Note .env files
# aren't shell-expanded, so "~" won't work below -- use the real absolute
# path (echo $HOME to check it) same as sync-tls-cert.sh's own output told
# you when it ran.

# TLS_CERT_FILE=/etc/pki/tls/certs/somehost.crt        # only works rootful
# TLS_KEY_FILE=/etc/pki/tls/private/somehost.key        # only works rootful
# TLS_CERT_FILE=/home/you/kingdom-proxy-tls/fullchain.pem   # rootless, after sync-tls-cert.sh
# TLS_KEY_FILE=/home/you/kingdom-proxy-tls/privkey.pem      # rootless, after sync-tls-cert.sh
